WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.170
<i>When I take an image</i>

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.131
[shutter click]

00:00:07.215 --> 00:00:08.508
<i>music just plays in my head.</i>

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:10.009
<i>I don't know if that works
for everyone else,</i>

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:12.095
<i>but that's just how it works
for me.</i>

00:00:12.095 --> 00:00:15.265
I sound crazy,
but it's the honest truth.

00:00:15.265 --> 00:00:18.601
[uplifting piano music]

00:00:21.563 --> 00:00:23.440
<i>The thing about photography
that I particularly love</i>

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.692
<i>is just being able
to like,</i>

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:28.153
<i>capture a moment</i>

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:28.153 line:92%
[shutter click]

00:00:30.739 --> 00:00:32.323
<i>and then other people
will be able</i>

00:00:32.323 --> 00:00:35.994
<i>to feel exactly what you felt
when you took the picture.</i>

00:00:44.836 --> 00:00:47.797
<i>[talking and camera sounds]</i>

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:02.437 size:88% position:44% line:60%
I like this because it's
kind of like a perspective

00:01:02.437 --> 00:01:05.064 align:start position:0% line:53%
of what you probably do
when there's nobody here.

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:07.400
<i>(Sarah)
I feel like photography
allows me to show</i>

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.526
<i>the beautiful side of New Haven</i>

00:01:08.526 --> 00:01:10.904
<i>as well as the real side
that other people need to see</i>

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:12.822
<i>to make all of it beautiful.</i>

00:01:12.822 --> 00:01:17.160 line:68%
I used to attend Achievement
First Amistad High on Dixwell.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.329 align:start size:53% position:47% line:71%
I'm 18 years old,

00:01:19.329 --> 00:01:21.706 align:start size:72% position:28% line:71%
and I love photography.

00:01:21.706 --> 00:01:23.416 align:start position:0%
This one's my favorite

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.668
<i>The thing with Amistad
is that at Amistad</i>

00:01:25.668 --> 00:01:28.505
<i>it's a college prep school,
so they don't really focus</i>

00:01:28.505 --> 00:01:30.882
<i>particularly on the arts
programs.</i>

00:01:30.882 --> 00:01:34.052
<i>So as far as a photography club
or a photography class,</i>

00:01:34.052 --> 00:01:35.386
<i>there was nothing of the sort</i>

00:01:35.386 --> 00:01:37.013
so I was really kind
of frustrated

00:01:37.013 --> 00:01:40.016
to not be able to have a space
to share with other kids

00:01:40.016 --> 00:01:42.101
and other colleagues
and other people

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:44.979
in the community of our skills
and our artistic sides.

00:01:44.979 --> 00:01:48.983
[traffic sounds]
[soft music]

00:01:53.112 --> 00:01:54.697
<i>(Martina)
I think I've become more aware</i>

00:01:54.697 --> 00:01:57.367
<i>of the role that the museum
could play in the community</i>

00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:59.452 size:88% position:44% line:71%
and that we actually need to

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:02.831 align:start position:0% line:68%
come out and be more proactive
in what we offer

00:02:02.831 --> 00:02:05.208 align:start position:0% line:68%
to people that feels
relevant to them

00:02:05.208 --> 00:02:07.252 align:start position:0% line:68%
and that feels like
a point of connection.

00:02:09.546 --> 00:02:11.589
<i>The View From Here began</i>

00:02:11.589 --> 00:02:14.133
<i>because I was curating
an exhibition</i>

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:18.346
<i>with Paul Messier at the
Institute for the Preservation
of Cultural Heritage</i>

00:02:18.346 --> 00:02:21.307
<i>about the artist Bill Brandt
and the artist Henry Moore</i>

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:23.977
<i>and how they came together
through photography.</i>

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:25.687
(Sarah)
My counselor was like: hey,

00:02:25.687 --> 00:02:28.273
there's this photography program
that Yale is throwing

00:02:28.273 --> 00:02:29.858
and they're interested
in some students

00:02:29.858 --> 00:02:31.276
and you know, you should apply.

00:02:31.276 --> 00:02:34.237
(Martina)
We opened a competitive
application system

00:02:34.237 --> 00:02:37.407
where we invited students
who are enrolled in

00:02:37.407 --> 00:02:38.950
what we called
greater New Haven.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:42.203
High school students
and first year college students

00:02:42.203 --> 00:02:44.998
and we thought we might get
a mix of people who are

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:48.042
at that point in their lives
where they're thinking about

00:02:48.042 --> 00:02:49.002
<i>what they want to do.</i>

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:50.587
<i>(Sarah)
I applied, I got an email</i>

00:02:50.587 --> 00:02:53.882
<i>a couple days later saying
that we saw your application</i>

00:02:53.882 --> 00:02:55.091
<i>and we would like
to interview you</i>

00:02:55.091 --> 00:02:57.135
<i>to be a part of the internship
and I was shocked</i>

00:02:57.218 --> 00:02:59.345
because I didn't do this
seriously,

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:01.389
because I didn't think
I'd be called back.

00:03:01.389 --> 00:03:04.183
We had a really good response
to the call for applications

00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:07.687
from a huge variety of schools
in the greater New Haven area.

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:09.731
It was exactly
what we hoped for.

00:03:09.772 --> 00:03:12.400
It was like a roller coaster
of emotions.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:14.277
It was like from I'm not
taking this seriously

00:03:14.277 --> 00:03:16.863
to I'm super excited that
I actually got into the program

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:19.824
and then from there,
it was just a great time.

00:03:19.824 --> 00:03:21.868 line:50%
Hi, Sarah.

00:03:19.824 --> 00:03:21.868 align:start position:0% line:0%
[Zoom bell sound]

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.578 size:84% position:58% line:78%
Hi Bob! How's it going?

00:03:23.578 --> 00:03:25.872
<i>(Sarah)
I absolutely love
all of the instructors there.</i>

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:27.957
<i>I absolutely love Bob Hixon.</i>

00:03:27.957 --> 00:03:33.004 align:end position:100% line:68%
Sarah was very impressive,
as a person

00:03:33.004 --> 00:03:36.007 align:start size:78% position:22% line:71%
and also her photography.

00:03:36.007 --> 00:03:38.635 align:end position:100% line:72%
(Sarah)
I think this was shot at
the lowest that my lens can go.

00:03:38.635 --> 00:03:40.428 align:start size:56% position:44% line:78%
I have a 1.4 lens.

00:03:40.428 --> 00:03:43.306 align:end position:100% line:76%
So I was like, let me experiment
with that aperture.

00:03:43.306 --> 00:03:47.101 align:end position:100% line:76%
This is one of my favorites
that you did this year.

00:03:47.101 --> 00:03:50.229
<i>(Bob)
Sometimes they taught me
when it comes</i>

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:53.191
<i>to content
and meaning and story.</i>

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:57.195
They were very good
with telling stories

00:03:57.195 --> 00:03:59.948
in their photographs,
which is something that

00:03:59.948 --> 00:04:04.327
that I admire and
I'm not always very good at it.

00:04:04.327 --> 00:04:06.913
<i>(Sarah)
With Bob, on the outside
he can seem, you know,</i>

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:10.875
<i>intimidating and very serious
but I got to see the artistic,</i>

00:04:10.875 --> 00:04:12.210
<i>you know, emotional,</i>

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:14.295
sentimental side of him
that allowed me

00:04:14.295 --> 00:04:17.590
to be more comfortable with
reaching out to him as well.

00:04:18.174 --> 00:04:20.051
<i>(Martina)
The process for
gathering our team</i>

00:04:20.051 --> 00:04:22.345
<i>that was teaching the course was</i>

00:04:22.345 --> 00:04:24.013
<i>I mean in a way,
it sort of mirrored</i>

00:04:24.013 --> 00:04:26.474
<i>the process of thinking
about what we want to do</i>

00:04:26.474 --> 00:04:27.725
<i>for the community.</i>

00:04:27.725 --> 00:04:30.645
What's our own community here
within the museum?

00:04:30.645 --> 00:04:33.523
We have photographers,
you know, who've been

00:04:33.523 --> 00:04:36.859
practicing photography
for years, decades.

00:04:36.859 --> 00:04:40.113
So we wanted to bring them in as
they're experts in photography.

00:04:41.406 --> 00:04:43.992 align:start size:50% position:50% line:78%
That background.

00:04:43.992 --> 00:04:47.161 align:end position:100% line:76%
That's a dynamite
treatment there.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:51.416
<i>(Bob)
Teaching on behalf of Yale</i>

00:04:51.416 --> 00:04:54.127
<i>can be a little daunting.</i>

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:55.962 align:end position:100% line:60%
Thank you! I really
appreciate that!

00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:59.882
<i>But her reaction filled me
with confidence</i>

00:04:59.882 --> 00:05:02.677
that alright,
I can do this, she's connecting.

00:05:02.677 --> 00:05:03.970
Ever since the program started

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:05.471
I've been just
dreaming of the day

00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:06.806
that we'll
all be able to meet up.

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:08.599
It would be really cool
to see the people

00:05:08.599 --> 00:05:11.227
that had that impact on me
and that gave me the opportunity

00:05:11.227 --> 00:05:13.646
to venture out
on my photography side

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:14.981
when I didn't
have the opportunity

00:05:14.981 --> 00:05:16.691
to do that in school.

00:05:17.066 --> 00:05:20.028
[Bright synth music]

00:05:28.453 --> 00:05:30.913
<i>(Martina)
I'm so excited
for this exhibition.</i>

00:05:30.913 --> 00:05:31.873
<i>We're going
to invite the students</i>

00:05:31.873 --> 00:05:35.043
<i>to come to a meet and greet,
a private viewing</i>

00:05:35.043 --> 00:05:36.669
<i>of the exhibition in person.</i>

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:38.838
<i>So we'll meet them in person
for the first time.</i>

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:41.382 align:start size:91% position:9%
It's really amazing to
see you. You look wonderful.

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:41.382 align:start size:50% position:50% line:85%
Oh so do you!

00:05:41.382 --> 00:05:42.717 align:start size:91% position:9%
Thank you!

00:05:42.717 --> 00:05:45.678
[upbeat synth music]
[laughing]

00:05:46.596 --> 00:05:49.015 size:81% position:41% line:85%
Yo! This is crazy!

00:05:49.015 --> 00:05:50.266 line:78%
It's good right?

00:05:50.266 --> 00:05:51.476
<i>(Bob)
You know, after dark</i>

00:05:51.476 --> 00:05:56.189
<i>to see these beautiful images
projected into the windows,</i>

00:05:56.189 --> 00:06:00.401
<i>I hope that they are
all thrilled when they
see their work there.</i>

00:06:00.735 --> 00:06:02.945 size:84% position:42% line:83%
It looks amazing.
Like absolutely stunning.

00:06:02.945 --> 00:06:05.782 align:end position:100% line:83%
Well, we appreciate the trust
you put in us because,

00:06:05.782 --> 00:06:08.576 align:end position:100% line:83%
you know, it was an experiment
for us as well.

00:06:08.576 --> 00:06:10.453 align:start size:88% position:13% line:92%
Oh, hi, Bob.

00:06:08.576 --> 00:06:10.453 align:start size:44% position:56% line:71%
oh here's Bob!

00:06:10.453 --> 00:06:13.372 line:71%
I would hug you if I could.

00:06:10.453 --> 00:06:13.372 align:start size:88% position:13% line:92%
I know! Elbow!

00:06:13.372 --> 00:06:15.625 align:start size:91% position:9% line:83%
How's it going?
It's been such a long time.

00:06:15.625 --> 00:06:17.502 line:88%
It's been a minute
since we've spoken.
Yeah!

00:06:17.502 --> 00:06:18.753 line:78%
You're also very tall, too.

00:06:18.753 --> 00:06:20.797 align:start size:94% position:6% line:83%
I didn't think you're going
to be this tall.

00:06:18.753 --> 00:06:20.797 align:end size:94% position:94% line:91%
Yeah!
[laughing]

00:06:23.508 --> 00:06:26.594 line:76%
It's just nice to see that we
get our work somewhere.

00:06:26.594 --> 00:06:28.221
<i>(Sarah)
The way that we're
able to communicate</i>

00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:30.306
<i>and look at our pictures
as if we did all this in person</i>

00:06:30.306 --> 00:06:33.518 size:88% position:56% line:88%
is I guess it speaks
to the experience of
photography and art.

00:06:33.518 --> 00:06:37.313 align:end size:94% position:94% line:91%
Like, although we did it
online, we're here in person,

00:06:37.313 --> 00:06:39.774 align:end size:94% position:94% line:83%
and the feelings are natural
and it's just great.

00:06:39.774 --> 00:06:40.900 line:92%
I think it's amazing.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:44.070
<i>(Martina)
I hope that the students
will take away from this course,</i>

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:47.824
<i>a sense of self-confidence
in their own artistic abilities,</i>

00:06:47.824 --> 00:06:50.034
<i>their own artistic discernment</i>

00:06:50.034 --> 00:06:53.287
and I know from conversations
that I've had with some

00:06:53.287 --> 00:06:56.290
of the students that they see
photography differently now.

00:06:56.290 --> 00:07:00.002
<i>(Bob)
These students, Sarah
and the others</i>

00:07:00.002 --> 00:07:04.423
<i>have so much going on,
are so capable in many ways</i>

00:07:04.423 --> 00:07:09.971
that I think they're all
destined to do great things.

00:07:09.971 --> 00:07:13.599
If I had a little bit to do
with that, that's great.

00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:14.851 line:57%
Congratulations to you!

00:07:14.851 --> 00:07:16.310
[clapping and cheering]

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:17.895
<i>(Sarah)
I will definitely remember
this moment in my life</i>

00:07:17.895 --> 00:07:20.565
<i>as life changing,
and not to be melodramatic,</i>

00:07:20.565 --> 00:07:23.442
but in all honesty,
it did change my life.

00:07:23.442 --> 00:07:26.612 align:end position:100%
To think that my pictures,
somebody from New Haven,

00:07:26.612 --> 00:07:28.948 align:end position:100%
somebody who goes to a
charter school down the street

00:07:28.948 --> 00:07:30.324 align:start size:47% position:53%
<i>has the ability</i>

00:07:30.324 --> 00:07:32.410 align:end position:100%
<i>to have their pictures
on the building.</i>

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:34.453
<i>It's a very emotional feeling.</i>

00:07:34.453 --> 00:07:37.498 align:end position:100%
<i>It's very, it makes me happy
and makes me proud</i>

00:07:37.498 --> 00:07:40.042 align:end position:100%
<i>and it makes me
feel accomplished.</i>

00:07:40.835 --> 00:07:44.088
[upbeat synth music]

00:08:16.954 --> 00:08:19.498 align:start size:6% position:94% line:0%
♪♪

